job|Paid position and ordinary task are separated because sorting books need not be an employment position. Only paid-work receives the Oxford ordinal; noun countability and Vietnamese distinctions checked.
primitive|Equipment example avoids the demeaning cultural description in source material. Basic development rather than merely ancient is the intended meaning; the heating detail is preserved in Vietnamese.
theatre|Building and art-form meanings have separate ordinal support. Countable location versus uncountable art checked, including regional spelling without canonical alias approval; costume context matches art sense.
whereby|Formal relative process linker is preserved under the ledger ADVERB evidence, with construction uncertainty left for review. Vietnamese theo đó has its antecedent in the sentence and not an incomplete gloss.
diagnose|Medical identification and technical fault identification remain distinct. The fictional medical sentence gives no treatment advice; patient/condition valency and the loose speaker connection align in translation.
